# CountUp - a number whose digits roll to their value, keeping its exact format (“2.4M”, “94 %”, “12,400”, “$1.2M”).
# roll "view" (default): rolls up from zeros the first time it comes into view (a landing). roll "change": still on the
# first paint, rolls whenever `to` changes (a dashboard; StatCard uses it for its value). It takes the size of what
# holds it; instant with reduced motion.
#   Stat(label: "appointments a month") { CountUp(to: "12,400") }      StatCard(…, value: total)  → rolls when total changes
# shadcn-for-muten · Custom · host JS count-up.js.
part CountUp(to: text, roll: text = "view") { Custom CountUp inputs(to: $to, roll: $roll) class("cx-countup") }
